+### UPDATED: `scripts/write-run-params.sh`
+
+Before adding the new parser rejection tests, replace the `--manual-gate-b` value
+read that currently relies on Bash `${2:?--manual-gate-b requires a value}` with the
+same explicit validation shape used by nearby value-taking flags:
+
+```bash
+--manual-gate-b)
+    if [[ $# -lt 2 || -z "${2-}" ]]; then
+        larch_err "--manual-gate-b requires a value"
+        exit 2
+    fi
+    MANUAL_GATE_B="$2"
+    shift 2
+    ;;
+```
+
+Rationale: the existing `${2:?...}` expansion exits before the script's explicit
+`larch_err` / `exit 2` path, so `assert_rejected_with` would fail on return code.
+This keeps the public error text unchanged while making missing and empty values
+testable through the script's normal validation contract. Do not broaden this patch
+to unrelated parser flags unless the local parser already uses a shared helper; the
+feature gap here is specifically `--manual-gate-b`.
 
